          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">What about grain filler?</h3>

          <p>
            Grain filler is a separate category worth knowing about: a thin paste spread over open-grained wood such as oak before finishing, so the surface ends up glass-smooth. A few wood fillers, Goodfilla in particular, can be thinned to do that job. Most cannot, and grain filling is not what most homeowners have in mind when they ask for wood filler.
          </p>
