        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            DAP Plastic Wood-X is the everyday filler most homes need: easy to apply, clear about when it is ready to sand, and dependable inside and out under paint. Switch to Minwax Stainable or Goodfilla for stained repairs, to Minwax High Performance or KwikWood for quick, strong exterior fixes, and to Abatron WoodEpox when rot has eaten away real wood.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Matching the product to the damage matters more than the brand on the tub. Filler goes in holes, putty in finished stained work, caulk in moving joints and epoxy in rot. Build fills in layers, sand them flat, prime every patch and stop the water that caused the damage, and the repair will outlast the paint on top of it.
          </p>
